  "security_implications": "valid_q controls the validity of sideloaded keys. Clearing it when en_i is low or clr_i is high can cause denial of service or mask key‑invalidation errors. Unintended assertion of set_i could mark an invalid key as valid, leading to use of incorrect secret material. The clear‑over‑set precedence may be exploited if input timing is not carefully managed, potentially dropping a legitimate key load. Loss of valid_q while key data persists is a secret leakage risk if the flag is later spuriously re‑asserted.",
